[
    {
        "content": "<p>Consider the following <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The generated name is `fun_continuous_mul'` -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_mul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: `continuous_fun_mul''` has already been declared -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_mul''</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_mul''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I want my lemma to have a <code>to_fun</code> version, but I want to choose the name of the lemma because by default it places <code>fun</code> at the beginning of the name, while I want it to be just before <code>mul</code>. But if I use <code>to_additive</code> I do not seem to be able to choose the name I want.</p>",
        "id": 619542057,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1787836891
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's possible that interaction between to_additive and to_fun hasn't been considered (sufficiently well) yet. CC <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span></p>",
        "id": 619542686,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1787837045
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also ran into this in a recent PR. What I did for the time being was to use <code>to_fun</code> with manual naming on the decls, and then add the <code>to_additive</code> attribute after the fact to generate the other versions.</p>",
        "id": 619557623,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1787840338
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, that'll do the trick for now.</p>",
        "id": 619558201,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1787840466
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What about swapping the attributes? (as a workaround)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_mul''</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_mul''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_add''</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_mul''</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_add''</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619564123,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1787841764
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh that does work! Though in my case I also want to choose the name of the <code>to_additive</code> version, because the multiplicative one should use <code>div'</code> while the additive one should use <code>sub</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo_fun_div'</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo_div'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Div</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousDiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">div'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo_sub'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- should be `foo_sub`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619565722,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1787842113
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, <code>to_fun</code> and <code>to_additive</code> can be used in either order. This gives you some freedom in naming the new declarations, but it doesn't let you specify the names of all 3 new declarations separately. The same issue would arise when combining <code>to_additive</code> with <code>to_dual</code> (which we don't do yet). Suggestion for what the syntax for this would look like are welcome.</p>",
        "id": 619848937,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1787937373
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What I would like to be able to write (but I don't know if it is possible) is:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_mul</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which would create a <code>continuous_fun_mul</code> lemma, and translate both <code>continuous_mul</code> to <code>continuous_add</code> and <code>continuous_fun_mul</code> to <code>continuous_fun_add</code>.</p>\n<p>And for the case where I need to name all 3 lemmas differently, I would be ok with something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to_fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_div'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_fun_sub</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_sub</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_div'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Div</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousDiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">div'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619850918,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1787937985
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I claim that if you want to manually name all three lemmas then you should not be trying to generate them all with a single attribute line.</p>",
        "id": 619877433,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1787945420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since <code>to_additive</code> naming is mostly very accurate (and it seems much harder to do this feasibly for <code>to_fun</code>), I think that you should just swap the order of the attributes as mentioned upthread.</p>",
        "id": 619877976,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1787945596
    }
]